  "body": "From the review of PR #105 (#96). Both the sideways rapid law and #96's new vertical law test only the tool CENTRE column (rest.in_stock(a), surface_before(a, i)). A dive whose centre is just outside the stock outline while the tool's circle (radius r) overlaps it is not caught; a dive whose centre lies within r of an earlier cut reads as cleared while its far side can still be uncut (e.g. an adaptive re-entry at a new XY on the next level). Not a regression (the sideways law has the same gap), but a missed collision.\n\nDone means: rapid-in-stock samples the tool's footprint (disk of radius r - gouge_tol), not just its centre, for both the sideways and vertical rapids; pinned by a dive r off a stock wall and a re-entry beside an earlier cut.",
